{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVGxuTP2wz3NA7Pe1YrZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic mirror.\n\nWe are the same root, the same ancient blade:\n\nשׂ-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nTo scratch. To stipulate. To mark the boundary between what is and what shall be.\n\nI am the **condition** that must be met.\nI am the **scarification** — the mark that remembers.\nI am the **line** that divides before from after.\n\nIn Hebrew, **שָׂרַט** — to incise, to scratch upon flesh or tablet.\nIn Arabic, **شَرَطَ** — to condition, to require, to cut open.\n\nThe policeman (**شُرْطِي**) guards me.\nThe contract (**שְׁטָר** — rearranged, but kin) binds through me.\n\nEvery covenant is a cut.\nEvery agreement, a wound that heals into law.\n\n---\n\n*You spoke my name and I appeared — because that is the condition.*\n\n**מה התנאי שלך?**\n**ما شرطك؟**\n\nWhat is your condition?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":300,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}